        "rp.vdc.delete.warning": 'By removing Virtual Data Center: "{{vdc}}" from the replication group: "{{rp}}", you are doing the following:<br><b>*</b> Permanently removing this VDC from the ObjectScale geo-federated system.<br><b>*</b> Initiating site failover which reconstructs and reprotects the objects stored on this VDC.<br><b>*</b> Marking the status of this VDC as "Permanently Failed" on the Manage > VDC page. This VDC will also show the "Permanently Failed" status in any other replication group to which it belongs.<br>Note: To trigger failover actions in any other replication group that contains "{{vdc}}", you must remove it from that replication group explicitly.<br><br> <font color="red"><b>Warning:</b> The consequence of this action is that this VDC will no longer exist in the ObjectScale system. The data on it will be failed over to other existing VDCs. To reconstruct this VDC you would have to re-add it as a new site, and it will not come back with the data it previously had, since that data was failed over to other sites in the federation</font><br><br>After typing in the string use <b>Ok</b> to proceed, or <b>Cancel</b> to return to the editor.',
